In article <161@bucsb.UUCP> dino@bucsb.UUCP (T.H.) writes:
> >I was playing 'hack' the other day when I was about to starve to death.
> >I went into a shop and steped on a food ration.  I was too weak to 
> >pick up the food ration so I ate it off the floor.  I went to the
> >entrance of the shop and paid the shopkeeper but it said "You don't owe
> ><shop keepers name> anything."  I thought this was strange so I ate 
> >another food ration off the floor and the same happened again.
> 
> That's in the newest version (1.0.3) as well.  Think of it as a feature.
> You can eat things even when you can't pick them up; without this feature
> it would be very difficult to eat dragon corpses.  It's something
> the shopkeeper doesn't catch.  He also doesn't charge you for what the dog
> eats.

The "you don't owe anything" message must have come because you were
holding no other food rations. In a recent game, I tried it and the
following happened... I ate one food ration off his floor, but was
holding 4 (already paid for- I had them when I came in). He charged me for
the four I was holding.

This is in PC-Hack 1.0.3. (an early version).

